{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795430399,"nonce":"0oicG+ARLcG+lfOIQgg8425jmYo=","title":"A scrollbar fade still full-paints when the container cannot be held","message":"939d7bd5 draws an auto-hiding scrollbar each frame apart from the batch, so its fade is a fast-path frame, but only when nothing above its container can move it. Recording the transform and clip at paint time is only right while those stay put. Its fade is still a full paint per frame when:\n\n- the container is inside another scroll container (a list in a scrolled page), or under a bound node, an animating node, a motion container or an overlay root;\n- any overlay is open at the paint, because the held scrollbars are drawn above the main content, and an open dropdown or toast has to cover them.\n\nWays out: chain the held scrollbar to its ancestors' poses as rows chain a bound node, so a moving ancestor moves it; and draw held scrollbars in the main band below the overlay content rather than after the dynamic batch. 3b364ef (scrolling as rows) lists the scrollbar thumb as its own row, which covers the first.\n\nRelated: add9f78, 3b364ef.","files":null}]}